                            <comment id="17683726" author="JIRAUSER298472" created="Fri, 3 Feb 2023 08:03:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Data query permission refers to whether the user has the permission to view the data in the table. Belongs to data permissions. Restrictions are required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sampling and reloading tables are operations on tables. Belongs to administrative permissions. There are no restrictions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the user does not have data query permission in the project, the actual sampled data will not be returned in the following interface&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;GET&lt;/tt&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://host:port/kylin/api/tables&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://host:port/kylin/api/tables&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13055099/13055099_image-2023-02-03-16-03-25-075.png&quot; height=&quot;197&quot; width=&quot;245&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17685090" author="jira-bot" created="Tue, 7 Feb 2023 07:09:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Commit 79b7b13a3859052765c81471140545a2abc10378 in kylin&apos;s branch refs/heads/kylin5 from binbin.zheng&lt;br/&gt;
[ &lt;a href=&quot;https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf?p=kylin.git;h=79b7b13a38&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf?p=kylin.git;h=79b7b13a38&lt;/a&gt; ]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5413&quot; title=&quot;After the user is turned off the data permission, the sampled data can still be seen&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;KYLIN-5413&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;KYLIN-5413&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; disable sample data when has no data query permission&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
